### Session 2 IPL: the Author routes.
### Use the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy these into Postman.

### All authors (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/authors

### One author (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/authors/3

### An id that matches nothing (404)
GET http://localhost:3000/authors/999

### An id that is not a number (400)
GET http://localhost:3000/authors/abc

### Add an author (201). The client supplies the id, because no primary key is IDENTITY.
POST http://localhost:3000/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": 900, "name": "Edgar Allan Poe" }

### Change an author's name (200, or 404 if the id does not exist)
PUT http://localhost:3000/authors/900
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "E. A. Poe" }

### Remove an author (204, no body, or 404 if the id does not exist)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/authors/900
